1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,699
Your universe has places, sides, and work.

2
00:00:04,599 --> 00:00:07,116
What it doesn't have yet is a story.

3
00:00:08,916 --> 00:00:11,739
Right now the crew can see every lead you wrote,

4
00:00:12,189 --> 00:00:14,581
from the first minute, in any order.

5
00:00:15,481 --> 00:00:16,871
That's a list of places.

6
00:00:18,671 --> 00:00:21,017
Today you turn it into chapters,

7
00:00:21,467 --> 00:00:23,698
where each one opens the next.

8
00:00:24,598 --> 00:00:26,398
And then you write the last page.

9
00:00:27,598 --> 00:00:31,192
Before I open the file, I write the story as three lines.

10
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:37,725
One. The crew finds the third colony's ship, and she's been stripped.

11
00:00:38,625 --> 00:00:42,131
Two. The miners' ledger says who sold her cargo.

12
00:00:43,031 --> 00:00:46,481
Three. That leads to a place the Gleaners won't talk about.

13
00:00:48,281 --> 00:00:52,103
Each line ends with something the crew has just learned.

14
00:00:53,003 --> 00:00:55,941
That's what makes it a chapter, and not an errand.

15
00:00:57,141 --> 00:00:59,437
You know these lines from Class One.

16
00:01:00,337 --> 00:01:04,270
Starts when, revealed, means the chapter is hidden.

17
00:01:05,170 --> 00:01:08,564
And Then, reveal, wakes the one with that key.

18
00:01:10,364 --> 00:01:12,557
So the first chapter keeps, at once,

19
00:01:13,007 --> 00:01:15,747
and gets one new line that points at the second.

20
00:01:16,646 --> 00:01:19,427
The second is new. It's hidden,

21
00:01:19,877 --> 00:01:21,815
and it points at the third.

22
00:01:23,615 --> 00:01:26,550
And the third was already here as a lead.

23
00:01:27,450 --> 00:01:30,691
I change at once to revealed, and give it a reward.

24
00:01:32,491 --> 00:01:34,503
Now read down the Then lines.

25
00:01:35,403 --> 00:01:37,898
That's your table of contents.

26
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:41,056
The words under a beat are the briefing.

27
00:01:41,956 --> 00:01:45,893
They're what the crew reads in the Quest Log when the chapter appears.

28
00:01:47,693 --> 00:01:50,179
A good one says what was just learned,

29
00:01:50,629 --> 00:01:52,424
and where to go next.

30
00:01:53,324 --> 00:01:57,187
And I mean where. I've written the place into the sentence.

31
00:01:58,987 --> 00:02:00,504
That matters for this chapter,

32
00:02:00,954 --> 00:02:03,270
because it doesn't end at a place.

33
00:02:04,170 --> 00:02:05,280
It ends on a signal.

34
00:02:06,180 --> 00:02:08,120
So Helm has nothing to engage,

35
00:02:08,570 --> 00:02:10,796
and the crew gets there by reading.

36
00:02:12,596 --> 00:02:16,392
And a briefing is a page, so it can hold more than the order.

37
00:02:17,292 --> 00:02:21,037
At the top, the Tern herself, drawn beside the words.

38
00:02:21,937 --> 00:02:25,024
Under the order, a table of what the crew found.

39
00:02:26,824 --> 00:02:28,634
The next one starts with a face,

40
00:02:29,084 --> 00:02:31,273
the Assay Office reading out the entry.

41
00:02:32,173 --> 00:02:36,000
That's a real face, written out in full, so copy every bit of it.

42
00:02:36,900 --> 00:02:39,281
And a heading, with no square brackets,

43
00:02:39,731 --> 00:02:41,908
for the thing the ledger leaves out.

44
00:02:43,708 --> 00:02:45,698
Keep the order in the first paragraph.

45
00:02:46,598 --> 00:02:49,727
A crew in a hurry reads that, and flies.

46
00:02:50,927 --> 00:02:54,183
Done when, signal, ledger read.

47
00:02:55,083 --> 00:02:58,736
Nothing sends that signal yet, so I write the thing that does.

48
00:03:00,536 --> 00:03:04,290
It's a call to the miners, like the two calls from Lecture Four.

49
00:03:05,190 --> 00:03:07,981
And there's one new item among an answer's outcomes:

50
00:03:08,431 --> 00:03:10,347
signal, and the same word.

51
00:03:12,147 --> 00:03:13,733
Now look at both answers.

52
00:03:14,633 --> 00:03:17,301
They both send it, so either one closes the chapter.

53
00:03:18,201 --> 00:03:20,336
But one pays the fee, politely,

54
00:03:20,786 --> 00:03:22,666
and the miners think better of the crew.

55
00:03:23,566 --> 00:03:25,331
The other demands the page,

56
00:03:25,781 --> 00:03:26,939
and they think worse.

57
00:03:28,739 --> 00:03:30,626
That's how a beat shifts standing.

58
00:03:31,526 --> 00:03:34,733
The deed goes in the answer, beside the signal.

59
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:38,914
You could write the deed on the beat itself.

60
00:03:39,814 --> 00:03:41,924
There's a line for it, called standing,

61
00:03:42,374 --> 00:03:44,612
and a beat's reward can hold one too.

62
00:03:46,412 --> 00:03:49,269
A deed on the beat goes to every ship in the game,

63
00:03:49,719 --> 00:03:51,801
whoever finished it, and whichever way.

64
00:03:52,701 --> 00:03:55,964
A deed in an answer goes to the ship that gave the answer,

65
00:03:56,414 --> 00:03:58,187
and to nobody else.

66
00:03:59,987 --> 00:04:01,680
So ask yourself what you want.

67
00:04:02,580 --> 00:04:05,139
If it's the story's verdict, put it on the beat.

68
00:04:06,039 --> 00:04:08,603
If it's a choice, put it in the answer.

69
00:04:09,503 --> 00:04:10,749
Here it's a choice.

70
00:04:11,949 --> 00:04:13,958
A goal is a beat with one more line.

71
00:04:14,858 --> 00:04:16,516
Win, and then a sentence.

72
00:04:18,316 --> 00:04:21,171
When this quest is done, the game ends,

73
00:04:21,621 --> 00:04:24,121
and that sentence is on the last screen.

74
00:04:25,021 --> 00:04:28,403
Citation is printed under it, on that same screen.

75
00:04:30,203 --> 00:04:31,779
My goal is hidden too,

76
00:04:32,229 --> 00:04:34,120
and the third chapter reveals it.

77
00:04:35,020 --> 00:04:38,533
So the ending arrives when the story has earned it.

78
00:04:40,333 --> 00:04:42,497
I save, and lint says clean.

79
00:04:43,397 --> 00:04:45,834
Lint is good at chains.

80
00:04:46,284 --> 00:04:48,719
It'll tell you when a chapter can never appear.

81
00:04:49,919 --> 00:04:53,051
Three entries at the start, and no sign of the rest.

82
00:04:54,851 --> 00:04:56,397
I go and find the Tern.

83
00:04:57,297 --> 00:04:59,456
And there's chapter two, with its briefing.

84
00:05:01,256 --> 00:05:05,141
It says to ask at the Assay Office, so that's where I go.

85
00:05:06,041 --> 00:05:08,247
I hail them, and I pay the fee.

86
00:05:10,047 --> 00:05:12,047
The chapter's done, it paid me,

87
00:05:12,497 --> 00:05:14,920
and the miners like me a little more.

88
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:17,156
And here's chapter three.

89
00:05:18,356 --> 00:05:20,758
This is the place the Gleaners won't talk about.

90
00:05:21,658 --> 00:05:24,245
And as I arrive, the goal appears.

91
00:05:26,045 --> 00:05:27,909
Four of them, and it's over.

92
00:05:29,709 --> 00:05:32,000
There's my sentence, on the last screen.

93
00:05:32,900 --> 00:05:34,772
And my citation, under it.

94
00:05:36,572 --> 00:05:37,935
One thing before you go.

95
00:05:38,835 --> 00:05:40,780
A universe doesn't have to end.

96
00:05:41,680 --> 00:05:45,360
Leave the goals out, and it's a sandbox for as long as the crew likes.

97
00:05:46,260 --> 00:05:48,686
Write a goal when your story has a last page.

98
00:05:49,886 --> 00:05:50,889
Now it's your turn.

99
00:05:51,789 --> 00:05:54,420
Write your story as three lines on paper first.

100
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:58,815
Chain them, with the first one open and the rest hidden.

101
00:06:00,615 --> 00:06:02,789
End one chapter with a conversation,

102
00:06:03,239 --> 00:06:06,592
and give the crew two ways to get what they came for.

103
00:06:07,492 --> 00:06:09,543
Then decide whether your universe ends.

104
00:06:11,343 --> 00:06:13,218
Next time, we put people in it.
